From 14f88dca92d43be0461d7b53d2f53827fb65a914 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: faycal <faycalelhandi9@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:24:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/26] perf(agc): bind GPU-produced draw buffers in place; CPU
 access trap for staged results

APS5_DRAW_SKIP_GPU_SNAPSHOTS=1: MarkDirectWrites records each range a dispatch wrote (in place or by
GPU copy-back) with its write generation, and PrepareDrawBindings binds a draw's read-only buffer in
place instead of copying a CPU snapshot of it when the range is such a GPU result and the CPU has not
written it since.

APS5_RESIDENT_TRAP=1 (measurement): RecordCopyBacks makes the copied-back pages of staged regions
PAGE_NOACCESS through the new libc GuestArenaTrap exports; the crash handler restores a faulting page
and counts the access by its first caller outside ucrtbase. On the Astro Bot world map no access came
from game code; 85% came from Recorder::refreshDrawSnapshot and 12% from CompareSpansFrom.

World map, same scene: presents 105-106 -> 107-111 per 10 s, GPU idle gaps 31 -> 25 ms per frame;
screenshot correct.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
